%! A household: all its members live in the same home.
%!
%! This file is a module. A program uses it with `@use household`, binds
%! the input `member` to one of its own predicates, and reads the output
%! `livesAt`. The home is the blank node _:home, which is a different one
%! for each use of the module.

@input member(person: any) .

livesAt(?person, _:home) :- member(?person) .

@output livesAt .
